{
  "id": "A02",
  "goal": "S1-04A",
  "title": "Room access: invitations by link, QR and email; a lobby where guests wait; sessions on the room calendar",
  "why": [
    "The founders asked to bring people into a room by QR code or an emailed invitation, to have them wait until someone lets them in, and to set when a session starts. The pack names membership invitation as product work and has no lobby or calendar.",
    "Guests reach the call only, never project records: they are admitted into a lobby entry, not the membership. A member invitation is bound to one email and adds its accepter as an editor or viewer, moving the audience revision.",
    "Invitation tokens travel in request bodies and URL fragments, never in paths or query strings, so no server or proxy logs them. Only their SHA-256 is stored.",
    "The lobby and sessions are shared project state, so the snapshot carries them and members see changes live through the event stream. The caller's role is per-person, so it has its own read (getProjectMembership) and the snapshot stays identical for every member."
  ],
